sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant MessageStore_Alice@{ "type" : "database" } as Message store (Alice)
    participant NodeState_Alice@{ "type" : "database" } as Node state (Alice)
    participant PayloadState_Alice@{ "type" : "database" } as Payload state (Alice)
    actor Alice
    actor Bob
    participant MessageStore_Bob@{ "type" : "database" } as Message store (Bob)
    participant NodeState_Bob@{ "type" : "database" } as Node state (Bob)
    participant PayloadState_Bob@{ "type" : "database" } as Payload state (Bob)
    Note over Alice, Bob: batch data sync

    Note over Alice, Bob: Initial state<br/>MessageStore_Alice = [M1, M2, M3]<br/>MessageStore_Bob = [M1]<br/>NodeState_A->B = {messages:[M1,M2,M3], offers:[], requests:[]}<br/>NodeState_B->A = {messages:[M1], offers:[], requests:[]}

    Alice->>PayloadState_Alice: create payload A->B {messages:[M1,M2,M3], acks:[]}
    Alice->>Bob: send payload A->B with messages
    Bob->>PayloadState_Bob: mark payload A->B as received

    Bob->>MessageStore_Bob: store missing messages M2 and M3
    Note right of Bob: Bob already has M1,<br/>so only new messages are added to MessageStore_Bob.
    Bob->>NodeState_Bob: update NodeState_B->A to {messages:[], offers:[], requests:[]}

    Bob->>PayloadState_Bob: add ACKs [M1, M2, M3] to payload A->B
    Bob-->>Alice: send ACK payload B->A
    Alice->>PayloadState_Alice: mark ACK payload B->A as received

    Alice->>NodeState_Alice: remove acknowledged messages from NodeState_A->B
    Note left of Alice: ACKs for M1, M2, M3 received.<br/>NodeState_A->B becomes {messages:[], offers:[], requests:[]}.

    Note over Alice, Bob: Final state<br/>MessageStore_Alice = [M1, M2, M3]<br/>MessageStore_Bob = [M1, M2, M3]<br/>NodeState_A->B = {messages:[], offers:[], requests:[]}<br/>NodeState_B->A = {messages:[], offers:[], requests:[]}